{
	"$comment": "Step -> model routing for ai/core.mjs callModel(), chosen by the benchmark in ai/bench/ (2026-10-15; tables, numbers and reasons: ai/research/benchmark.md). Every thinking step runs on Claude Opus 5.5 (the user's preference, confirmed or matched by the measurements), at the reasoning effort the benchmark found best for that step: observe medium (end to end on the picture cases, 2 samples x 26: pass 0.96 vs 0.90 at low, +11 s), plan medium, refine medium, edit low (for plan, high was no better and slower; for edits, medium/high changed things the user did not ask for). Route: claude-group (Anthropic-native: prompt caching of the catalog, 0 errors in ~1,500 bench calls). Fallbacks: the same model on AWS Bedrock (an independent backend; no strict json_schema there, which these steps do not use), then a different family measured as the best fast stand-in for that step. retries 1 per route: a hung or failing route moves on to an independent backend quickly instead of retrying it twice. timeoutMs is about 3x the slowest answer measured for the primary; budgetMs leaves room for one fallback. models: per-route quirks (vision, prompt caching via cache_control on the system prompt, params the route rejects).",
	"version": 2,
	"defaults": {
		"retries": 1,
		"backoffMs": 1500,
		"maxBackoffMs": 20000,
		"timeoutMs": 120000,
		"budgetMs": 300000,
		"minAttemptMs": 8000
	},
	"models": {
